    "reproductionProcedure": "# Exact TREE FORCE function archive recovery\n\nRecovered the original `treeforce89-dev` archive without editing an active checkout, changing dependencies there, or making a deployment/database request.\n\n- Repository: `TheCryptoArborist/tree-token.xyz`\n- Immutable source: `bc6545db57714d4ac18f50243fbcce72755cad5e`\n- Original deploy: `6ae56c08df52d066dfb245ed`\n- Required and recovered bytes: **1,753,127**\n- Required and recovered SHA256: **725fe5a7e7ff30c2c83f7b6a1bf1af534a72ee2efa1cc6faf64151743cf84905**\n- Archive: `source/.netlify/treeforce89-paid-release/private-functions/treeforce89-dev.zip`\n- Verification: `recovery-report.json`\n\n## Reproducible procedure\n\n1. Export the exact commit from `https://codeload.github.com/TheCryptoArborist/tree-token.xyz/tar.gz/bc6545db57714d4ac18f50243fbcce72755cad5e` into an isolated `source/` directory. No Git metadata is needed.\n2. Read that commit's `AGENTS.md` and `production/README.md`. This recovery uses only the historical TREE FORCE package step; it does not invoke a general build, frontend build, release script, runtime configuration change, or upload.\n3. From `source/`, install the two original dependency locks:\n\n   ```sh\n   npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund --loglevel=error\n   npm ci --prefix netlify/preview-lib/treeforce89-source --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund --loglevel=error\n   ```\n\n4. **Remain in the repository root**, then run `node ../recover.mjs`. The helper invokes the exact `zipFunctions` call from `scripts/prepare-treeforce89-paid-release.mjs` at the source commit:\n\n   ```js\n   await zipFunctions(root + '/netlify/canonical-development-functions', output, {\n     archiveFormat: 'zip',\n     config: { '*': { nodeBundler: 'esbuild', nodeVersion: '22.x' } },\n     basePath: root,\n   });\n   ```\n\n5. Require the complete ZIP size and SHA256 above before the archive is used.\n\nThe pinned packager is `@netlify/zip-it-and-ship-it` 16.3.0. The nested TREE FORCE Sui SDK is 2.37.0. Both package manifests and both lockfiles were compared with the immutable source archive after installation and remained byte-identical. Runtime is `nodejs22.x`, invocation mode `stream`, bootstrap 2.24.0; metadata is recorded in the report.\n\n## Deterministic working-directory detail\n\nThe first invocation ran from the parent of `source/`, producing a ZIP ten bytes larger. Its single changed payload entry contained esbuild labels prefixed with `source/`. Running from the repository root produced the exact original ZIP digest. The failed attempt is retained as `attempt-1.zip` and `attempt-1-report.json`; it must not be used for a release. `recover.mjs` now rejects an incorrect working directory.\n"
